From f1a13faa1f9837678f085f6dad9c18a51dad3b36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Liberty <mliberty@precisioninno.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 03:14:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] python: name every Bazel SWIG module <tool>_py

odb, utl, gpl and wmk were the only Bazel modules not named <tool>_py, a
leftover from when they were standalone extensions. Name them odb_py,
utl_py, gpl_py and wmk_py as CMake does, so every extension in
_openroad.so is _<tool>_py and the loader needs no special cases. The
package paths stay (src.odb.odb_py), since other generated wrappers import
odb and utl through them; `import odb` and `import utl` are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Matt Liberty <mliberty@precisioninno.com>
